This is a new, non-trivial module (it traverses the navigation state to locate the persistent Domain sidebar route and keeps it in sync before navigating), but it opens straight into `import`s followed by the `getActiveDomainSidebarRoute` function with no header comment describing the file's purpose. A reader has to reverse-engineer what the module is for from its two functions. There is a JSDoc line on `navigateToDomainSettingsRoute`, but the file itself has no top-level description.

Add a short header comment at the top of the file describing what it does and why it exists, for example:

```ts
/**
 * Keeps the persistent wide-layout Domain sidebar pointed at the destination Domain when the Search Router
 * navigates across Domains, so the sidebar and page title stay in sync with the opened Domain settings route.
 */
import Navigation from '@libs/Navigation/Navigation';
// ...
```

